                "name": "dipikabh",
                "url": "https://github.com/dipikabh"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 145 adds support for the Crash Reporting API; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6228675846209536\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6228675846209536</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have documented this as part of the Reporting API documentation, rather than in its own API docs tree, as I feel that this makes much sense, even though it is specified in a separate spec.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
