        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6210057?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">getDay() range incorrectly mentioned as one-indexed (1-7) instead of zero-indexed (0-6)</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixing typo/incorrect content</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Change suggested based on getDay() docs:<br>\n<a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/getDay#:~:text=An%20integer%2C%20between%200%20and%206%2C%20representing%20the%20day%20of%20the%20week%20for%20the%20given%20date%20according%20to%20local%20time%3A%200%20for%20Sunday%2C%201%20for%20Monday%2C%202%20for%20Tuesday%2C%20and%20so%20on\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date/getDay#:~:text=An%20integer%2C%20between%200%20and%206%2C%20representing%20the%20day%20of%20the%20week%20for%20the%20given%20date%20according%20to%20local%20time%3A%200%20for%20Sunday%2C%201%20for%20Monday%2C%202%20for%20Tuesday%2C%20and%20so%20on</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43781",
            "title": "Fixed typo in getDay() range - was 1-7 now 0-6",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T03:55:49.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-14T03:55:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "coryannj",
                "url": "https://github.com/coryannj"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The recommendation for using <a href=\"https://github.com/fregante/browser-extension-template\">browser-extension-template</a> to set up an extension project was removed from the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/Build_a_cross_browser_extension\" rel=\"nofollow\">Build a cross-browser extension</a> page in October 2022. At that time, the template was updated to Manifest V3, but the how-to page has not been updated.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The how-to page has been updated to cover Manifest V3, so the recommendation can be restored.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes #121826</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43777",
            "title": "Issue 21826: Restore browser-extension-template recommendation",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T00:06:25.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-14T00:04:47.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62723358?u=f3632393d0193c912fa572def786f97a3e49c40b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/style-src-attr#violation_cases\" rel=\"nofollow\">Content-Security-Policy: style-src-attr directive &gt; Examples &gt; Violation cases</a>, change the style attribute value to something that does not use a keyword.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I intend to avoid possible confusion. A user might think <code class=\"notranslate\">style-src-attr 'none'</code> blocks <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;div style=\"display:none\"&gt;Foo&lt;/div&gt;</code> because it has \"none\" in the attribute value. (At least one user was confused… me.)</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43775",
            "title": "docs: change inline style example to avoid confusion",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T23:32:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T23:29:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wesleyboar",
                "url": "https://github.com/wesleyboar"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 146 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTextureUsage</code>; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728</a>, and also see <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds documentation for the new usage type.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43773",
            "title": "Technical review: Document TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT usage",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T17:55:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T17:53:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 146 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">texture_and_sampler_let</code> WGSL feature/extension. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5102334940151808\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5102334940151808</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR documents this extension.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">cc/ <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/beaufortfrancois/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/beaufortfrancois\">@beaufortfrancois</a></p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43768",
            "title": "Technical review: Document texture_and_sampler_let WGSL feature",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T15:04:57.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T15:03:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome has added support for two features that allow sites to size fonts in proportion to the operating system/browser text scale settings:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;meta name=\"text-scale\" content=\"...\" /&gt;</code> element, which was added in Chrome 146, and works across Desktop and Mobile platforms. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112244702674944\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112244702674944</a>.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">preferred-text-scale</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">env()</code> variable, which was added in Chrome 138. This only really works in Android,</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR documents both of these features.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43766",
            "title": "Technical review: Document meta text-scale and env(preferred-text-scale)",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-16T09:27:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T13:09:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF150 adds support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/script/type/importmap#merging_multiple_import_maps\" rel=\"nofollow\">multiple import maps</a> behind a pref (<code class=\"notranslate\">dom.multiple_import_maps.enabled</code>). This adds an experimental feature and release note entry.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It also adds a minor clarification to the JS doc.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127672727\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43551\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43551/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43551\">#43551</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43759",
            "title": "FF150 Expr Feature - multiple JS import maps",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-15T13:46:54.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T07:06:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118266?u=5a7fb2f3d1ecc7dcd73f43f4b478cb4938e6572c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds docs for the <code class=\"notranslate\">shadowrootslotassignment</code> attribute.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Trying to add the docs so that <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4083478419\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12267\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/12267/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12267\">whatwg/html#12267</a> can be merged.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've largely cribbed the docs style from the other <code class=\"notranslate\">shadowroot*</code> attributes.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4247549777\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29457\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29457/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29457\">mdn/browser-compat-data#29457</a></p>",
